                "F": {
                    "text": "effect on frequency: no effect, effect on wavelength: increase",
                    "math_alt": [],
                    "plain_text": "effect on frequency: no effect, effect on wavelength: increase"
                }
            },
            "correct_answer": "B",
            "correct_answer_raw": "effect on frequency: decrease, effect on wavelength: increase",
            "correct_answer_plain": "effect on frequency: decrease, effect on wavelength: increase",
            "correct_answer_images": [],
            "explanation": "Gamma rays have very high frequency and very short wavelengths. Microwaves have lower frequency and longer wavelengths. This could also be deduced from the idea of expansion. The expansion of the universe stretches the wavelengths of electromagnetic (EM) waves so wavelengths have increased with time. All EM waves travel at the speed of light so an increase in wavelength must be accompanied by a decrease in frequency because c = f l.\nTherefore the answer is B.",
            "explanation_images": [],
            "extracted_at": "2026-07-04T23:56:17.473186",
