            "explanation": "The rate of conduction along a copper cylinder is determined by its cross-sectional area A, its length l and the temperature difference (T2 – T1) between the two ends. If we change one of these quantities, the rate of conduction will also change.\nIn case H, the temperatures of both ends of the bar increase by the same amount and so here, there is no change to the temperature difference or to either of the other quantities. As a result, the rate of conduction of thermal energy does not change and is the same as the value for bar X.",
